      "target": "../sections/sec-106-annex-1-development-of-the-national-health-workf.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "the National Health \nWorkforce Accounts\nNational Health Workforce Accounts: A Handbook\nThe list of National Health Workforce Accounts (NHWA) indicators was developed through a \nstepwise process that included several phases of consultation on preselected indicators.\n \nIn October 2015, over 450 indicators were selected from diverse sources of international and \nsubregional literature and filtered down to a set of 255. The filtering process was executed to \nremove duplicates by eliminating multiple indicators that capture the same underlying concept \n(data), as well as to embrace all recommended",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes in Annex 1 the multiphase consultative process used from 2015 to 2017 to filter over 450 candidate metrics down to 78 core NHWA indicators through Technical Advisory Group reviews, expert scoring on relevance and feasibility, and global public consultation.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
