      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "+ Annex 2: Indicator metadata sheets +",
      "pageStart": 139,
      "pageEnd": 141,
      "target": "../sections/sec-107-annex-2-indicator-metadata-sheets.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "National Health Workforce Accounts: A Handbook\nThe indicators in the National Health Workforce Accounts (NHWA) are specified in the metadata \nsheets outlined in Part II of this Handbook. The indicators are mostly numeric (quantitative), i.e. \nrepresenting in numbers certain ratios with a numerator and denominator related to a human \nresources for health (HRH) policy field. There are also capability indicators on the existence of \ncertain regulations, processes, etc. reflecting the status of development of the HRH manage-\nment system of a country. The metadata sheets aim to provide a definition",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Explains in Annex 2 the structure and fields of the Part II indicator metadata sheets, defining indicator numbering, numerator and denominator specifications, disaggregation categories, capability scoring questions, data reporting frequency, and potential data sources.",
