      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Example 1: Self-sustainability of the health workforce",
      "pageStart": 142,
      "pageEnd": 144,
      "target": "../sections/sec-109-example-1-self-sustainability-of-the-health-work.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "As advocated by the WHO Global Code of Practice on the International Recruitment of Health \nPersonnel, all Member States should strive to create a self-sustainable health workforce and \nwork towards establishing effective health workforce planning, education and training, and \nretention strategies that will reduce their need to actively recruit migrant health personnel. \nHence, policies and strategies addressing national self-sustainability are distinguished as \na 2030 milestone in the Global Strategy on Human Resources for Health: “All countries are \nmaking progress towards halving their depe",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Presents Example 1 in Annex 3 on monitoring national health workforce self-sustainability, showing how indicators from Modules 1, 2, 4, 5, 6, 7, 9, and 10 are combined to assess domestic training output against reliance on foreign-trained personnel.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "antigravity",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-30"
      }
