      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Example 3: Required health worker training performance",
      "pageStart": 146,
      "pageEnd": 149,
      "target": "../sections/sec-111-example-3-required-health-worker-training-perfor.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "performance \nThe national supply of new health workers to the health labour market is key to the success \nof any health policy. The implementation of educational plans is a determinant that requires \ncareful monitoring, and is a key element in the Global Strategy on Human Resources for Health \npolicies, articulated through several milestones:\n•\t (by 2020); “All countries have inclusive institutional mechanisms in place to coordinate an \nintersectoral health workforce agenda”\n•\t (by 2020); “All countries have established accreditation mechanisms for health training \ninstitutions”\n•\t (by 2030);",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Presents Example 3 in Annex 3 on monitoring required health worker training performance, showing how indicators across Modules 2, 3, 4, 5, 9, and 10 track the educational pipeline from accreditation and financing to graduate entry into practice.",
